item.content:encoded:
This joint event of the San Francisco LightHouse for the Blind and Visually Impaired and the San Francisco Public Library features scientist and designer Josh Miele in conversation with author Jason Roberts. Together SFPL and SFLH invite library patrons and the broader Bay Area LightHouse community to come together in celebration of Dr. Miele’s new memoir, “Connecting Dots – A Blind Life.” The evening features an on-stage interview, audience questions, light nosh, and book signing.

&nbsp;

Josh Miele is former president of the LightHouse Board, and has mentored and collaborated with their MAD Lab on many innovative tactile maps projects. His memoir includes stories about his development of TMAP and the tactile BART Station Maps that are near and dear to the LightHouse community.

&nbsp;

Miele is honored to be in conversation with Jason Roberts, author of perhaps the best book ever written about a historical blind hero, “A sense of the World – How a Blind Man Became History’s Greatest Traveler.” His most recent book is “Every Living Thing – The Great and Deadly Race to Know All Life.”

&nbsp;

This event and conversation promise to be next-level fun and fascinating – get your tickets while they last!
